    body_en: "In my second year of university, I started my first part-time job at a cafe. During busy hours I often made mistakes because I was overwhelmed. Once I took an order wrong and apologized to the owner several times. Over time, my hands got quicker and I learned tricks for dealing with customers. There were hard days, but I still can't forget the joy of receiving my first paycheck. I remember buying my parents a small gift with that money. Working part-time taught me firsthand how hard it is to earn money. Since then, I've become more careful whenever I buy something. I think that experience greatly helped shape who I am today.",
