    title_kr: "냉장고 파먹기",
    title_en: "Eating through the fridge",
    body_kr: "냉장고를 열어 보니 유통기한이 임박한 재료들이 여기저기 쌓여 있었다. 그동안 장을 볼 때마다 필요 이상으로 사는 습관이 있었던 것 같다. 그래서 이번 주는 장을 보지 않고 냉장고에 있는 재료만으로 요리를 해 보기로 했다. 처음에는 재료가 애매해서 무엇을 만들지 고민이 많았다. 남은 채소와 고기를 모두 넣어 볶음밥을 만들었더니 의외로 맛있었다. 다음 날에는 남은 두부와 계란으로 간단한 반찬을 만들었다. 냉장고를 정리하면서 그동안 잊고 있었던 재료들도 발견했다. 일주일이 지나니 냉장고가 훨씬 깔끔해지고 지출도 줄어들었다. 앞으로는 필요한 만큼만 장을 보는 습관을 들여야겠다고 다짐했다.",
    body_en: "When I opened the fridge, I found ingredients piled up here and there, close to their expiration dates. I seem to have had a habit of buying more than necessary every time I went grocery shopping. So this week, I decided to cook using only the ingredients already in the fridge instead of shopping. At first, I had trouble deciding what to make since the ingredients were mismatched. I put all the leftover vegetables and meat into fried rice, and it turned out surprisingly tasty. The next day, I made a simple side dish with leftover tofu and eggs. While organizing the fridge, I also discovered ingredients I had forgotten about. After a week, the fridge was much tidier and my spending had decreased too. I resolved to develop the habit of buying only as much as I need from now on.",
    questions: [
      { question_en: "Why did the narrator decide not to shop this week?", options: ["The fridge was full of near-expired ingredients","The store was closed","A friend suggested it","No money left"], answerIndex: 0 },
      { question_en: "What result did the narrator notice after a week?", options: ["The fridge was tidier and spending decreased","Nothing changed","Spending increased","The fridge was messier"], answerIndex: 0 },
    ],
